  "question": "The following is a business requirement description for a surveillance database system:\n\nThe system is used to manage cameras, video recordings, alarms, and events. System functions include camera management, video recording management, alarm and event recording, as well as real-time monitoring and historical query. The camera management module is responsible for storing camera titles, locations, RTSP stream addresses, and real-time video stream paths, while also recording camera analysis times. The video recording function includes storing the video file path, cover path, start time, and duration for each camera. The alarm management module records alarm information in videos, such as alarm type, level, start and end times, and allows quick retrieval of associated alarms via video ID. The event recording function records specific events in videos through coordinates and dimensions, as well as event type and occurrence time. In addition, the system supports real-time video monitoring via RTSP stream addresses and intelligent analysis based on camera analysis times to generate alarms and event records. With these records, the system supports data analysis functions such as event frequency statistics and alarm type analysis to help security personnel promptly identify and resolve issues. Historical query and security management functions also help trace events and address potential security risks.",
  "ddl": "-- Schema for database: rschema_0236\n\nCREATE TABLE `camera` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `title` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `location` varchar(255) NOT NULL,\n  `rtsp_stream_address` varchar(512) NOT NULL,\n  `realtime_video_path` varchar(512) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `analysis_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `video_recording` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `camera_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `file_path` varchar(512) NOT NULL,\n  `cover_path` varchar(512) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `duration` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `video_recording_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`camera_id`) REFERENCES `camera` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `alarm` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `video_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `alarm_type` varchar(128) NOT NULL,\n  `alarm_level` varchar(64) NOT NULL,\n  `start_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `end_time` datetime DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `video_id` (`video_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `alarm_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`video_id`) REFERENCES `video_recording` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;\n\nCREATE TABLE `event` (\n  `id` int(11) NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,\n  `video_id` int(11) NOT NULL,\n  `event_type` varchar(128) NOT NULL,\n  `occurrence_time` datetime NOT NULL,\n  `coord_x` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `coord_y` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `width` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  `height` int(11) DEFAULT NULL,\n  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),\n  KEY `video_id` (`video_id`),\n  CONSTRAINT `event_ibfk_1` FOREIGN KEY (`video_id`) REFERENCES `video_recording` (`id`) ON DELETE CASCADE ON UPDATE CASCADE\n) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb3;",
